NODE id=matrix/construct/projection.ProjectEvent kind=func
  digest=b3:a256bd6025b0ba7789d43b0ddb6edaee45bfef308f815ba665d0ea559db37c14 file=construct/projection/project.go range=54:73 lang=go exported=true byte_range=1321:2289
  sig=func ProjectEvent(ev Event) []*schema.Surface
  doc=ProjectEvent maps one normalized pipeline event onto zero or more Construct\nsurfaces (the PASSIVE tier — deterministic, no model). Pure + deterministic:\nthe same event in yields the same surfaces out (golden-testable), so a replay\nof the stored surface events reproduces them identically. An unrecognised\nevent yields nil — the projector stays silent rather than emitting noise.\n\nThe set of handled types is deliberately tight: the produced step text and\nthe tool result are the two high-value "dark-matter" wins documented in the\nfrozen spec ([coverage].tool_result) and the post-launch bug report (the\ntool-only-plan opacity). Richer typing of open-ended blobs is the agent's job\nvia the ACTIVE tier (RenderTools), not a heuristic guess here.
EDGES
  calls=matrix/construct/projection.projectStepText,matrix/construct/projection.projectToolResult
  references=matrix/construct/projection.Event,matrix/construct/projection.ev,matrix/construct/projection.projectStepText,matrix/construct/projection.projectToolResult,matrix/construct/schema.Surface
  ^calls=matrix/executor/cmd/mcl-execute.daemonState.projectConstructEvent
  ^references=matrix/executor/cmd/mcl-execute.daemonState.projectConstructEvent
  ^defines=matrix/construct/projection/project.go

