NODE id=matrix/construct/projection.encodePayload kind=func
  digest=b3:dcdbc00dd074bd8a728cdfc7ecc7242ff4b12d68486c6cf57860e68bb211c327 file=construct/projection/render.go range=192:208 lang=go exported=false byte_range=8910:9721
  sig=func encodePayload(v interface{}) ([]byte, error)
  doc=encodePayload turns the render arguments' `payload` into the JSON bytes the\nkind-matched primitive is decoded from. The payload is normally a nested JSON\nobject, but models frequently DOUBLE-ENCODE it as a JSON string (the whole\nobject stringified). In that case args["payload"] arrives as a Go string, and\nre-marshaling it would quote it AGAIN — yielding "cannot unmarshal string into\nGo value of type primitives.X" when buildSurface decodes it. Detect the string\ncase and use its bytes directly so a double-encoded payload still parses.
EDGES
  references=matrix/construct/projection.b,matrix/construct/projection.err,matrix/construct/projection.ok,matrix/construct/projection.s,matrix/construct/projection.v
  ^calls=matrix/construct/projection.ParseRender
